  "description": "Explore emergence in .NET: cellular automata (MergeLife, Life-like with its History and Super variants, Generations, Larger than Life, rule tables, Elementary, Cyclic, Wireworld), HashLife on an unbounded plane, three flavors of Lenia, fractals (Newton's basins, and Mandelbrot, Julia, and Burning Ship with deep zoom, to 1e9000 for Mandelbrot and Julia), Reynolds boids, and Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion under one consistent API, plus pattern files in every common format and a genetic evolver that searches for new MergeLife rules. Pure C#, netstandard2.1, zero dependencies: it runs anywhere .NET does, including Unity and IL2CPP, and its step and frame APIs allocate nothing. Every system follows a written specification and conformance vectors shared with the Python package, so the same parameters and seed give the same run in either language.",
